# Vendored trees must be byte-identical to upstream on every platform, and
# vendor.py's tree_sha256 hashes raw bytes. Git for Windows converts LF to CRLF
# on checkout by default, which changed every hash and failed `vendor.py check`
# on windows-latest while Linux and macOS passed.
#
# Disable end-of-line conversion repo-wide: whatever upstream committed is what
# lands on disk. Not `text=auto eol=lf`, which would still normalise on commit
# and so would rewrite a vendored file that legitimately contains CRLF.
* -text
